{"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/unitpoint"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI"]]},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/init(x:y:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/x","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/y"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/bottom","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/bottomLeading","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/bottomTrailing","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/center","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/leading","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/top","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/topLeading","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/topTrailing","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/trailing","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/zero"],"anchor":"Type-Properties","title":"Type Properties"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/Equatable-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations"}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A normalized 2D point in a view’s coordinate space."}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","title":"UnitPoint","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UnitPoint"}],"symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UnitPoint"}],"externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI9UnitPointV","modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"roleHeading":"Structure"},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/s15BitwiseCopyableP","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/SQ","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/SH","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/s8SendableP"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UnitPoint"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use a unit point to represent a location in a view without having to know"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the view’s rendered size. The point stores a value in each dimension that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indicates the fraction of the view’s size in that dimension — measured"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the view’s origin — where the point appears. For example, you can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"create a unit point that represents the center of any view by using the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.5"},{"type":"text","text":" for each dimension:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["let unitPoint = UnitPoint(x: 0.5, y: 0.5)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To project the unit point into the rendered view’s coordinate space,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"multiply each component of the unit point with the corresponding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component of the view’s size:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["let projectedPoint = CGPoint(","    x: unitPoint.x * size.width,","    y: unitPoint.y * size.height",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can perform this calculation yourself if you happen to know a view’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"size, or if you want to use the unit point for some custom purpose, but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftUI typically does this for you to carry out operations that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you request, like when you:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Transform a shape using a shape modifier. For example, to rotate a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shape with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Shape\/rotation(_:anchor:)"},{"type":"text","text":", you indicate an anchor point"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that you want to rotate the shape around."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Override the alignment of the view in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Grid"},{"type":"text","text":" cell using the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View\/gridCellAnchor(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" view modifier. The grid aligns the projection"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of a unit point onto the view with the projection of the same unit point"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"onto the cell."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a gradient that has a center, or start and stop points, relative"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the shape that you are styling. See the gradient methods in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"ShapeStyle","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can create custom unit points with explicit values, like the example"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"above, or you can use one of the built-in unit points that SwiftUI provides,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"like "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/zero"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/center"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/topTrailing"},{"type":"text","text":". The built-in values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"correspond to the alignment positions of the similarly named, built-in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Alignment"},{"type":"text","text":" types."}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A unit point with one or more components outside the range "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[0, 1]"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"projects to a point outside of the view."}]}],"style":"note","name":"Note"},{"type":"heading","text":"Layout direction","level":3,"anchor":"Layout-direction"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When a person configures their device to use a left-to-right language like","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"English, the system places the view’s origin in its top-left corner,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with positive x toward the right and positive y toward the bottom of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"view. In a right-to-left environment, the origin moves to the upper-right","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"corner, and the positive x direction changes to be toward the left. You","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"don’t typically need to do anything to handle this change, because SwiftUI","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"applies the change to all aspects of the system. For example, see the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"discussion about layout direction in ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/HorizontalAlignment"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It’s important to test your app for the different locales that you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"distribute your app in. For more information about the localization process,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"see ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/Xcode\/localization","type":"text"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/s8SendableP":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/s8SendableP","title":"Swift.Sendable"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/UnitPoint/leading":{"title":"leading","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"leading","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UnitPoint","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI9UnitPointV"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A point that’s centered vertically on the leading edge of a view.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/unitpoint\/leading","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/UnitPoint\/leading"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/UnitPoint/Equatable-Implementations":{"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI